  "preserved_failures_and_corrections": [
    "Legacy standard single-precision MKL fails one original 36-case production-size error comparison; this existing control failure is retained in all three fresh warm runs.",
    "Final private-in-place single-precision FFTW route passes 34/36; maximum-error failures remain disqualifying and no timing is accepted for that route. CPU route exploration is closed.",
    "V4 test campaign exposed native Triton correlation-AD absence in both baseline and candidate. Tests were corrected to preserve native parity and separately require derivatives through the supported Torch fallback; runtime implementation did not change for this correction.",
    "Executable v1 and v2 controllers stopped on reviewer-missed assumptions: standard scheme imports Torch, and full PSD bytes differ across schemes in the established references. Failed attempts remain immutable and are excluded from timing.",
    "V3 checks exact published science records by scheme plus exact candidate-own-baseline equality. PSD files are directly hashed; no tolerance or scientific operation changed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Shared-host fixed finite 384-template workload; three fresh process samples per role yield observed ranges, not confidence intervals.",
    "External frame/bank and remote source identity were checked by pinned acquisition and receipts; replay verifies those receipt pins and prior independently reviewed source hash maps.",
    "Conditioned strain was captured as raw-data hash metadata; replay verifies equality of those records. PSD arrays and trigger HDF files are directly reread and compared.",
    "Warm FFT timings and the 1,920-call surrogate are separate diagnostics, not executable throughput or forecasts.",
    "Profile and trace durations are overlapping instrumented attribution, not additive speedup budgets.",
    "Native CUDA correlation autograd remains an existing limitation; passing fallback derivative tests does not claim native support.",
    "Related native suite has one platform skip: unavailable MPS on Linux, inferred from the test guard and sole recorded skip; the quiet log itself does not print the skipped test identity."
  ]
